; iter_non_vec_register_empty_slice: an ITER whose register does not hold a
; vec raises even when the slice is empty and the body would not have run.
;
; ITER carries a `read` effect on its register that the verifier's static
; type system depends on, so skipping the loop without ever resolving the
; register discards that effect. spec/xqvm/ISA.md's ITER row orders the
; steps register-read-before-skip and its error clause has no emptiness
; carve-out.
;
; The register is filled from calldata rather than by STOW because that is
; the shape the verifier admits: xqvm/src/verifier/reg_type.rs gives INPUT
; the write type RegType::Any, which satisfies ITER's static requirement, so
; this program is verifier-clean and therefore admissible to a chain's
; store_program. Rust returned SkipLoop before the type arm, so it halted
; with outputs = [7] where the Python VM -- and 0.3.x -- faulted.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
PUSH 1           ; start_idx
PUSH 1           ; end_idx -- empty slice
ITER r0
NEXT

PUSH 7
STOW r1
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1
HALT
